# Parity wave, families lane (docs/development/parity/families.md): native Vulkan with the residue census, a Bink movie played in
# the world, Whiterun at noon (sky, sun glare query, water), the inventory (menu scene, its shadow masks), the map (local map), then
# Dragonsreach. Every class the census still counts in these windows is a lost draw. Read the "[ORG] residue census" lines, the
# "[ORG] flush latch: engine" [E] lines, "[ORG] Bink:" lines (expect "movie ended: N frames drawn by the render graph, 0 by the
# engine"), "[ORG] occlusion queries: cs.sky.sun: ... 256 lease indices made at setup", and every "[DCLF] <family>: the engine draws"
# line (each names a refusal that is left).
# cs-ab: disable-mod=Skyrim Engine Telemetry
# cs-ab: disable-mod=ImprovedCameraSE
CS_ORG_NATIVE=1
CS_DISABLE_FEATURES=Upscaling
CS_ORG_RESIDUE_CENSUS=1
CS_ORG_RESIDUE_CENSUS_FRAMES=60
CS_ORG_RESIDUE_CENSUS_TOP=60
CS_ORG_BINK_SHOT=40,120
DXVK_DEBUG=hang
VK_LOADER_LAYERS_DISABLE=*nsight*
CS_DCLF_TEST_COMMANDS=500:dclf:shot=start;600:set timescale to 0;601:set gamehour to 13;700:coc Whiterun;1100:dclf:shot=whiterun;1150:dclf:bink=BGS_Logo.bik;1250:dclf:shot=after-bink;1300:dclf:menu=InventoryMenu=show;1450:dclf:shot=inventory;1500:dclf:menu=InventoryMenu=hide;1550:dclf:menu=MapMenu=show;1700:dclf:shot=map;1750:dclf:menu=MapMenu=hide;1800:coc WhiterunDragonsreach;2200:dclf:shot=dragonsreach
CS_DCLF_TEST_EXIT=2300
